To fix the CORS (Cross-Origin Resource Sharing) error in Next.js running on top of WordPress, you can follow these steps:

1. Install the necessary packages:

```bash
npm install cors axios
```

2. Add `cors` middleware to your server configuration in `pages/_app.js`. This will allow cross-origin requests from Next.js to your WordPress site:

```javascript
import Cors from "cors";
import type { AppProps } from "next/app";
import React from "react";
import { Provider } from "react-redux";
import store from "../store";
import axios from "axios";

const MyApp = ({ Component, pageProps }) => {
  axios.defaults.baseURL = process.env.WORDPRESS_API_URL;
  return (
    <Provider store={store}>
      <Component {...pageProps} />
    </Provider>
  );
};

MyApp.getInitialProps = async (appContext) => {
  // Calls to getInitialProps in pages and nested routes will be called before appCreateController
  const appProps = await App.getInitialProps(appContext);
  return { ...appProps };
};

// Wrap your entire application inside App with CORS middleware
export default (props) => {
  const cors = new Cors({
    methods: ["GET", "HEAD"],
  });

  return Cors(async (req, res) => {
    const handle = cors.handle;
    await handle(req, res, async () => {
      const preparedApp = MyApp(props);
      await preparedApp.getInitialProps(req, res);
      return preparedApp.render(req, res);
    });
  }).createServer();
};
```

3. Define the `WORDPRESS_API_URL` environment variable in your local development or production environments. This is the base URL of your WordPress REST API endpoint:

```json
